{"id":"5cdc9a86-bbbc-4e48-bf4d-5c829f8bfb4e","object":"chat.completion","created":1785022600,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        pid = n['parent']\\n        if pid is not None:\\n            children.setdefault(pid, []).append(n['id'])\\n    # find root\\n    root = None\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n['parent'] is None:\\n            root = n['id']\\n            break\\n    if root is None:\\n        raise ValueError('No root node')\\n    # compute subtree counts\\n    subtree_counts = {}\\n    def dfs(nid):\\n        counts = {}\\n        sym = node_map[nid]['symbol']\\n        counts[sym] = counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n        for child in children.get(nid, []):\\n            child_counts = dfs(child)\\n            for s, c in child_counts.items():\\n                counts[s] = counts.get(s, 0) + c\\n        subtree_counts[nid] = counts\\n        return counts\\n    dfs(root)\\n    total_counts = subtree_counts[root]\\n    removed_ids = set()\\n    removed_order = []\\n    # sort by depth desc, then id asc\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if not n['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        if nid == root:\\n            continue\\n        if n['symbol'] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n        # check all children are removed\\n        child_ids = children.get(nid, [])\\n        if any(cid not in removed_ids for cid in child_ids):\\n            continue\\n        # check required symbols remain\\n        sub_counts = subtree_counts[nid]\\n        feasible = True\\n        for req in required_symbols:\\n            if total_counts.get(req, 0) - sub_counts.get(req, 0) < 1:\\n                feasible = False\\n                break\\n        if not feasible:\\n            continue\\n        removed_ids.add(nid)\\n        removed_order.append(nid)\\n    retained_ids = [n['id'] for n in nodes if n['id'] not in removed_ids]\\n    retained_ids.sort()\\n    return {\\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_order,\\n        'retained_node_ids': retained_ids\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write a Python function `solve(case)` that implements grammar-guided node reduction as per the description. The case has fields: nodes (list of dicts with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility) and required_symbols (list of strings). The goal: decide which nodes to remove (if removable) and which to retain, while ensuring that required symbols are present after removal, and respecting the tree structure (parent-child). The algorithm: deeper nodes first (higher depth), then by stable tie-breaking using node ID. Tentatively remove a node if all required symbols remain represented (i.e., after removal, the set of symbols covered by retained nodes must include all required_symbols). Do not remove root, required symbol nodes, or nodes with retained children (i.e., if you remove a node, all its descendants must also be removed? Actually careful: The description says \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" That implies if a node has any child that is retained, you cannot remove that node. Also \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" So we need to decide which nodes to remove, processing in order (deeper first, then tie by id), and if a node is removable and not root, not a required symbol symbol (or is it the node itself? The node has a symbol, but required_symbols are symbols, not node IDs. So a node whose symbol is in required_symbols should not be removed. Also nodes that have any retained children cannot be removed.\n\nThis is reminiscent of the Perses algorithm: starting from full tree, consider removing nodes in bottom-up order. For each node, check if removing it (and all its subtree) still keeps required symbols present in the rest of the tree. Also ensure that the node is removable (property). If yes, mark it as removed. Then continue.\n\nWe need to output removed_node_ids (list in order of removal, presumably the order we processed and removed) and retained_node_ids (list sorted, maybe alphabetically? The description says \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\" So retained_node_ids should be sorted (likely lexicographically), and removed_node_ids should be in the order we removed them.\n\nImplementation steps:\n\n1. Parse case: nodes list, required_symbols list.\n2. Build a dict mapping node id to node dict.\n3. Build children mapping: parent -> list of children ids.\n4. Ensure root exists (parent null). Also note: root's symbol might be \"root\", but we treat it specially: never removable (explicit removable=false). Also required_symbols may include \"root\"; that's fine.\n5. We need to process nodes in order: sort nodes by depth descending, then by id ascending for tiebreak. Iterate in that order.\n6. For each node, check:\n   - If not removable, skip.\n   - If node is root (parent null), skip.\n   - If node's symbol is in required_symbols, skip (cannot remove a node that directly provides a required symbol).\n   - If node has any children that are retained (i.e., not removed), skip (cannot remove a node with retained children). Because removing this node would also remove its subtree, but if any child is retained, that implies the child is still present, so removal would orphan the child? Actually if we remove the node, all its descendants are also removed. So we cannot remove if any descendant is retained. But easier: check if any child is currently retained (not removed). Since we process depth-first from leaves up, if children are not removed yet, they might be considered later. But if we are